{"name":"Desert Rock","hex":"#d5c6bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert rock","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The music of the Palm Desert Scene, a Californian style of hard rock.","Synonym of stoner rock (“subgenre of heavy metal”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert_rock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Palm Desert Scene","blocks":[{"text":"The Palm Desert Scene is a group of related bands and musicians from Palm Desert, California that began in the early 1990s. Their hard rock sound – sometimes described as desert rock – contains elements of heavy metal, psychedelia, blues, punk, alternative, grunge, and other genres. It often features distinctive repetitive drum beats, a propensity for free-form jamming, and \"sludgy\" or \"trance-like\" grooves. The involved musicians often play in multiple bands simultaneously, and there is a high rate of collaboration between bands. The term \"stoner rock\" is sometimes used interchangeably with the term \"desert rock\". However, not all Palm Desert scene bands are \"stoner rock\" and not all stoner rock bands sound exactly like those in Palm Desert. Palm Desert has been named by Blender magazine as \"one of the top seven rock n' roll cities in America\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Queens_of_the_Stone_Age_-_SSE_Arena_Wembley_-_Saturday_18th_November_2017_QOTSAWembley181117-29_%2824730972488%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Queens_of_the_Stone_Age_-_SSE_Arena_Wembley_-_Saturday_18th_November_2017_QOTSAWembley181117-29_%2824730972488%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palm_Desert_Scene"},{"title":"Desert blues","blocks":[{"text":"Tishoumaren or assouf, internationally known as desert blues, is a style of music from the Sahara region of northern and west Africa. Critics describe the music as a fusion of blues and rock music from the United States, with Tuareg, Malian or North African music. Various other terms are used to describe it including desert rock, Saharan rock, Takamba, Mali blues, Tuareg rock or simply \"guitar music\". The style has been pioneered by Tuareg musicians in the Sahara region, particularly in Mali, Niger, Libya, Algeria, Burkina Faso and others; with it also being developed by Sahrawi artists in Western Sahara."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Tinariwen-Bardentreffen_2010.jpg/330px-Tinariwen-Bardentreffen_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_blues"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/1280px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A camel shepherd in southern Tunisia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/500px-Deserts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/1280px-Deserts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/500px-Deserts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The world's largest non-polar deserts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeserts.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Wallpaper_of_E-ELT_site_testing_%E2%80%94_Cerro_Armazones_Chile.jpg/500px-Wallpaper_of_E-ELT_site_testing_%E2%80%94_Cerro_Armazones_Chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th